__pycache__/
*.o
*.a
build/
out/

opencode.*
# built binaries
/saphira-llm
/saphira-llm-test
/saphira-llm-schedbench
# Disposable diagnostic: prints per-CPU timing evidence for the calibration
# claim in docs/PHASE6-BASELINE.md. The evidence is recorded in that document;
# the binary is not, and saphira-llm-tgbench / saphira-llm-kernelbench remain
# tracked by deliberate policy established in d96f361.
/saphira-llm-topoprobe
# saphira-llm-eval is a build product too. It is deliberately NOT tracked,
# unlike saphira-llm-tgbench and saphira-llm-kernelbench which d96f361 chose to
# keep: those two predate the .gitignore binary list and are an established
# (if odd) policy. A tool that did not exist at v0.0.1 has no such history, and
# a stale committed binary is worse than none. Its behaviour is gated by
# tests/test_eval.c, which does not need the binary committed to run.
/saphira-llm-eval
*.disasm
*.funcs

# models and scratch never belong in the repository
*.gguf
*.f32.tmp
*.log

# Local upstream investigation report: never committed or pushed with Saphira.
# The .gitignore entry may be committed; the report file itself stays untracked.
llama.cpp-bugreport.md
